cadtui localisation — command option-keyword probe (P3, CI/runner, hardest)

Parent: cadtui.issue (Phase 7). Harvest the localised OPTION KEYWORDS of CAD
commands and their per-locale abbreviation letters — the second distinct
dictionary (spec lines ~128-140, ~671-676). This is the hardest to harvest
because it requires driving each command's prompts to read back its keyword set
(note the PROMPTOPTIONTRANSLATEKEYWORDS sysvar).

What to collect
- Per (command . international-keyword): the local keyword and its local
  abbreviation letter.

How
- A probe suite (mirror the getcname probe pattern; soft cad-tagged jobs in
  .gitlab/native.yml, artifacts under dist/option-keywords/) that, for a NARROW
  set of common commands first, enters each command and captures its offered
  keywords in the localised install. Scope narrowly and expand later — do not
  attempt the whole command set at once.

Matrix
- Per vendor × locale × platform, aligned with the getcname probe; fr_FR first.

Output feeds cadtui-locale-data-format-and-loader.issue (option-keywords.sexp).
Missing entries fall back to the international keyword.

Priority P3: cadtui phases 1-6 do not need this; it refines Phase 7 once command
names (getcname) and aliases (.pgp) are in.

--- FINDING (2026-09-14): batch prompt-driving does NOT work ---

First attempt (MR !242 machinery, optkw-probe.lsp): drive each command with
PROMPTOPTIONTRANSLATEKEYWORDS on and capture the "[option/list]" from its prompt.
Run on the runners (pipeline 2845988706):

- AutoCAD / AcCoreConsole (fr): `(setvar "PROMPTOPTIONTRANSLATEKEYWORDS" 1)` is
  REJECTED ("paramètre de la variable AutoCAD rejeté") and the error escapes
  vl-catch-all-apply at the alfe protocol level, aborting the probe at that form
  before any command runs.
- BricsCAD /b (fr_FR, BRICSCAD 25.0): the setvar is accepted and all 13 command
  blocks run, but every block is EMPTY — `(command "_OFFSET")` in batch does not
  echo its option prompt to captured stdout (BricsCAD /b stdout is silent — the
  alfe-cad-probe playbook's known limitation; a LOGFILE is needed, itself broken
  on V26 macOS).

So option keywords are NOT harvestable by driving commands in a batch engine.
Viable directions to try instead:
  1. LOGFILE capture: LOGFILEMODE/LOGFILEON, run the commands, read the log back
     with a LISP-opened file (works around silent /b stdout).
  2. GUI automation (--mode automation) reading the prompt via a reactor/grread
     instead of stdout — heavier, Windows-only, dialog-risk.
  3. Parse the localised keyword tables out of the CUIX / resource files, if a
     readable mapping exists there (no command-driving, but vendor-specific).
The probe + wrapper + converter framework stays (MR !242); the CAPTURE mechanism
is what needs to change. No data landed (empty/aborted transcripts, not noise).


## First fr_FR harvest (2026-10-06, MR !440)

The first version of the probe never worked: it bracketed STDOUT, where a
command's prompt never arrives (empty blocks on BricsCAD V25 Windows / V26
macOS, jobs 16979749963 / 16979749962), and AutoCAD 2022's console aborted the
whole run at (setvar "PROMPTOPTIONTRANSLATEKEYWORDS" 1) even under
VL-CATCH-ALL-APPLY (job 16979749961). Reworked:

- the probe reads each command's prompt from the CAD's own command-history
  LOG (one fresh LOGFILEPATH directory per command), restoring the original
  LOGFILEPATH / LOGFILEMODE before printing; the keyword-translation setvar
  only when the variable exists; ZOOM last (entering it ended the
  accoreconsole run);
- the converter decodes the Windows wrapper's UTF-8-BOM + UTF-16LE
  transcript, repairs the cp437 mojibake of UTF-8 bytes (an e-acute arriving
  as U+251C U+2310), skips the log headers, and attributes each prompt to the
  command whose ECHO precedes it (BricsCAD writes its log lazily: a command's
  own log file starts with the previous command's tail).

