## AutoCAD re-run (2026-10-08, clautolisp 2.3.6): NOTHING NEW -- the 9th command ends the run

optkw:probe:accoreconsole:windows was re-run (job 16998925798, master pipeline
2922145991) with ZOOM moved last, to reach RECTANG, PLINE, BREAK, LENGTHEN.

What it harvested: EXACTLY the 2026-10-06 set and nothing more. The transcript
(dist/optkw/accoreconsole-Windows.txt: UTF-8 BOM + banner + UTF-16LE body,
decoded with the converter) holds the blocks of OFFSET, TRIM, EXTEND, FILLET,
CHAMFER, MIRROR, ROTATE, SCALE, then OPTKW-INCOMPLETE. Regenerated with the
converter, the harvest is identical, keyword for keyword, to the committed
probe-results/optkw/fr_FR/autocad-2022-windows.sexp (left as it is; same
OFFSET [Par/Effacer/Calque], TRIM/EXTEND [mOde], FILLET and CHAMFER lists).
MIRROR, ROTATE, SCALE again opened on a plain "Sélectionner des objets:" (no
bracketed list). So: no new local keyword, no new pair; --pair regenerates
fr_FR/option-keyword.sexp unchanged (57 pairs, 8 left to measure).

The diagnosis of 2026-10-06 was WRONG: ZOOM did not end the run. The run ends
after the 8th command, SCALE, whatever comes 9th -- ZOOM in job 16981155886,
RECTANG in job 16998925798. Timing (trace.log): the probe starts at
09:58:30Z, all eight logs carry the same second (11:58:36 local), and the job
then sits silent until the wrapper's alfe --timeout 300 expires (the probe
step ends 10:03:49Z). So the 9th command (or the 9th LOGFILEPATH redirection)
WEDGES the console; it does not crash it. Two readings remain, and this run
cannot tell them apart: (a) RECTANG and ZOOM each wedge accoreconsole, or
(b) something positional (9th fresh log directory / 9th command) does.

Probe adjusted (optkw-probe.lsp), to settle it on the next run:
- order: PLINE BREAK LENGTHEN first (never reached on AutoCAD), then OFFSET
  TRIM EXTEND FILLET CHAMFER MIRROR ROTATE SCALE, then RECTANG, ZOOM. A run
  stopping at the 9th command (now MIRROR, harvested twice) means (b); one
  stopping at RECTANG means (a); either way PLINE/BREAK/LENGTHEN come first.
- OPTKW-TRY <command> is printed BEFORE each command is entered (before the
  log redirection), so the transcript names the command a run died in. The
  converter ignores the line.
The family is optkw, so the jobs run automatically in the merge request
pipeline of this change (PROBES_CHANGED); a plain branch push does not.

REMAINS (unchanged otherwise)
1. BricsCAD "sélectionner les options (?)" (8 commands): needs an ENGLISH
   BricsCAD install.
2. AutoCAD 2022: RECTANG, PLINE, BREAK, LENGTHEN, ZOOM still NOT HARVESTED --
   re-run optkw:probe:accoreconsole:windows with the reordered probe, then
   pair them against the Autodesk English command reference as on 2026-10-07.
   MIRROR/ROTATE/SCALE: no bracketed first prompt (measured twice).
   BricsCAD V25: PLINE and LENGTHEN gave no bracketed prompt.
3. Other locales.


## Reordered run (2026-10-08, MR !461, clautolisp 2.3.6): LENGTHEN paired; the hang is not a command

Runs of the reordered probe (OPTKW-TRY markers): AutoCAD 2022 accoreconsole
job 17026576122, BricsCAD V25 Windows job 17026576124, BricsCAD V26 macOS job
17026576123.

What they harvested
- AutoCAD 2022: PLINE, BREAK, LENGTHEN, OFFSET, TRIM, EXTEND, FILLET,
  CHAMFER, MIRROR completed (then hung at ROTATE, below).
  NEW: LENGTHEN "Sélectionnez un objet à mesurer ou
  [DIfférence/Pourcentage/TOtal/DYnamique] <TOtal>:".
  PLINE "Spécifiez le point de départ:" and BREAK "Sélectionnez un objet:"
  offer NO keyword at their first prompt (measured; not missing data).
  The five already harvested are unchanged.
- BricsCAD V25 Windows: all 13 commands completed, OPTKW-DONE (no hang; the
  OPTKW-INCOMPLETE line in that transcript was the wrapper's false alarm:
  Select-String over the BOM + UTF-16LE report missed the OPTKW-DONE that is
  there -- fixed, the wrapper now checks the captured lines).
  NEW: LENGTHEN "[DYnamique/Incrément/Pourcentage/Total]" (the earlier run
  lost it: it was the LAST command, and BricsCAD writes a command's prompt
  into the NEXT command's log). PLINE "Origine de la polyligne :" offers no
  keyword. Every command the two runs share has the same keywords; ZOOM was
  last this time and so was lost here (kept from job 16981155888).
- BricsCAD V26 macOS: all 13 blocks empty, as before (no log in batch).

The converter now MERGES several transcripts of one product (first run that
offers keywords for a command wins; a differing later list is reported as a
CONFLICT, never silently preferred -- none here). The committed harvests are
regenerated from all runs:
  autocad-2022-windows.sexp  <- jobs 16981155886 16998925798 17026576122
  bricscad-v25-windows.sexp  <- jobs 16981155888 17026576124

New pairs (international <- local [local abbreviation]); count, order and
meaning agree with the English reference:
  AutoCAD 2022 _LENGTHEN  Delta <- DIfférence [DI]; Percent <- Pourcentage [P];
                          Total <- TOtal [TO]; Dynamic <- DYnamique [DY]
    https://help.autodesk.com/cloudhelp/2022/ENU/AutoCAD-Core/files/GUID-76C74C62-DBAA-41E7-8422-F0EE7E769638.htm
    (prompt headings: Object Selection, then Delta, Percent, Total, Dynamic;
    Delta Length / Total Length / Angle are their sub-prompts)
  BricsCAD V25 _LENGTHEN  DYnamic <- DYnamique [DY]; Increment <- Incrément [I];
                          Percent <- Pourcentage [P]; Total <- Total [T]
    https://help.bricsys.com/en-us/document/command-reference/l/lengthen-command?version=V25
    (options: DYnamic, edit Mode, Increment, Angle, Percent, Total -- "edit
    Mode" "returns to original prompt" and Angle belongs to Increment, so
    both are sub-prompt options; the first prompt's four agree in order)
option-keyword.sexp: 65 pairs (was 57), 8 left to measure (the "(?)" ones).
Tests: fr-option-keywords-lengthen-per-product (11 checks).

The accoreconsole hang, across the three runs
| job         | completed before the hang    | hung at |
|-------------+------------------------------+---------|
| 16981155886 | 8: OFFSET .. SCALE           | ZOOM    |
| 16998925798 | 8: OFFSET .. SCALE           | RECTANG |
| 17026576122 | 9: PLINE BREAK LENGTHEN .. MIRROR | ROTATE |
- Timing: every completed command's log has the start second (the probe
  begins ~8 s after accoreconsole is launched); then nothing until alfe's
  --timeout 300 (the step lasts 5 min 19-20 s in each run). A HANG, not a
  crash, and not a time limit.
- Not a particular command: ROTATE ran fine after MIRROR in the first two
  runs and hung after MIRROR in the third; ZOOM/RECTANG hung there only
  because they came 9th.
- Not the Nth command: 8, 8, then 9.
- Not state left by a predecessor: the last completed command differs
  (SCALE, SCALE, MIRROR) and each block ends on "Commande:" -- the cancel
  went through, no prompt left open; each command uses its own fresh
  LOGFILEPATH directory, restored before printing.
- BricsCAD runs the same 13 commands in one session without hanging.
- What fits: a CUMULATIVE OUTPUT limit. alfe launches accoreconsole with its
  stdout/stderr as pipes and reads them only after the process has exited;
  accoreconsole writes its whole command line (UTF-16LE) there. A pipe
  nobody reads blocks the writer once its buffer is full, at whatever
  command the total crosses it. The output before the three hang points is
  of the same order (3.6k-4.0k characters of probe output), but too roughly
  known to pin a capacity: SUSPECTED, filed as
  issues/open/alfe-accoreconsole-console-pipe-not-drained.issue (P1, with a
  confirming probe and the fix: drain the pipes while the engine runs).

Probe change (cheap, done): scripts/run-optkw-probe.ps1 runs accoreconsole
ONE SESSION PER COMMAND (13 sessions, --timeout 120 each), passing the
command in OPTKW_COMMANDS, which optkw-probe.lsp reads (comma-separated;
unset = the whole list, as BricsCAD runs it). Each session's console output
stays small, and a hang would cost one command, not the rest. If ROTATE,
SCALE, RECTANG and ZOOM then all complete, that also supports the pipe
hypothesis. The probe also ends with REDRAW, so BricsCAD's last real command
(ZOOM) has a successor to carry its prompt.

REMAINS
1. BricsCAD "sélectionner les options (?)" (TRIM, EXTEND, FILLET, CHAMFER,
   MIRROR, ROTATE, SCALE, BREAK; LENGTHEN does not offer it): needs an
   ENGLISH BricsCAD install.
2. AutoCAD 2022: RECTANG and ZOOM still NOT HARVESTED (ROTATE, SCALE
   measured earlier: no keyword) -- re-run optkw:probe:accoreconsole:windows
   with the per-command sessions, then pair against the Autodesk reference.
3. The alfe pipe ticket (confirm, fix).
4. Other locales.


