New pairs (AutoCAD 2022); count, order and meaning agree with the reference:
  _RECTANG  Chamfer <- Chanfrein [C]; Elevation <- Elévation [E];
            Fillet <- Raccord [R]; Thickness <- Hauteur [H]; Width <- Largeur [L]
    https://help.autodesk.com/cloudhelp/2022/ENU/AutoCAD-Core/files/GUID-188B2DDA-6CD8-4D37-BF26-E6CF27C34C75.htm
    (the page quotes the prompt itself: "Specify first corner point or
    [Chamfer/Elevation/Fillet/Thickness/Width]"; Hauteur is the extrusion
    height, i.e. Thickness -- Elevation has its own keyword)
  _ZOOM     All <- Tout [T]; Center <- Centre [C]; Dynamic <- DYnamique [DY];
            Extents <- ETendu [ET]; Previous <- Précédent [P]; Scale <- Echelle [E];
            Window <- Fenêtre [F]; Object <- Objet [O]
    https://help.autodesk.com/cloudhelp/2022/ENU/AutoCAD-Core/files/GUID-66E7DB72-B2A7-4166-9970-9E19CC06F739.htm
    (headings after the window corners: All, Center, Dynamic, Extents,
    Previous, Scale / Scale factor, Window, Object, then Real Time = the
    <temps réel> default, not a bracketed keyword)
option-keyword.sexp: 78 pairs (was 65), 8 left to measure.
Tests: fr-option-keywords-rectang-zoom-autocad (10 checks).

REMAINS
1. BricsCAD "sélectionner les options (?)" (TRIM, EXTEND, FILLET, CHAMFER,
   MIRROR, ROTATE, SCALE, BREAK): needs an ENGLISH BricsCAD install. The only
   unpaired keyword left of the 13-command scope.
2. Deeper prompts (the options offered after the first answer) are not
   driven; the scope is the first prompt of 13 commands.
3. BricsCAD V26 macOS writes no log in batch mode.
4. Other locales.
